    {
      "name": "Realtime (WebSocket)",
      "description": "The WebSocket feed at `{{wsUrl}}` cannot be run from this collection\n(see the collection description for why). Exercise it manually:\n\n### Connect\n\n1. **New → WebSocket Request** (not a request inside this collection).\n2. Enter `ws://localhost:8000/ws` and press **Connect**.\n3. On connect the server immediately pushes:\n\n```json\n{ \"type\": \"welcome\" }\n```\n\n### Observe a broadcast\n\n4. Keep the socket open.\n5. In this collection, run **Matches → POST /matches - live match (201)**.\n6. The WebSocket tab receives the created match:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"match_created\",\n  \"data\": {\n    \"id\": 1,\n    \"sport\": \"football\",\n    \"homeTeam\": \"Riffa\",\n    \"awayTeam\": \"Muharraq\",\n    \"status\": \"live\",\n    \"startTime\": \"2026-08-19T10:00:00.000Z\",\n    \"endTime\": \"2026-08-19T12:00:00.000Z\",\n    \"homeScore\": 0,\n    \"awayScore\": 0,\n    \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-19T11:00:00.000Z\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nEvery connected client receives this — open two WebSocket tabs to see the fan-out.\n\n### Messages\n\n| type | when | payload |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `welcome` | immediately on connect | none |\n| `match_created` | after a successful `POST /matches` | the full match row |\n\nThe server does not currently handle inbound client messages.\nMax payload is 1 MB; connections to any path other than `/ws` are rejected with 404.",
      "item": []
    }
  ]
